## General
Serving: [8 inch chiffon (Not enough)]

Prep Time: 20-30 minutes

Baking Time: 30 minutes

Oven: 350 F

Material: Electric batter, silicon spatula, flour filter, 2 mixing bowls, cake mold, 2 ceramic bowls

Difficulty: Medium

Can be used as chiffon, cupcake or any cake recipe.

## Ingredients
4 eggs
40g oil
40g milk
80g sugar
100g flour

lemon or orange juice (Optional)

## Instructions
Separate egg yolk and egg whites.


Egg yolk:
40g oil
40g milk
80g sugar
Mix in.
Filter 100g flour
Mix again.


Egg white:
Electric batter
Add lemon/orange juice
Add in 40g sugar in 3 small amounts. Fully batter before adding next
Whisk until soft tip naturally down.


Take some egg white batter into egg yolk batter, mix by lifting


Pour all egg yolk batter into egg whites. Lift mix.


Pour into cake mold

Put in oven.

## Tips

- Use two ceramic bowls to cool down the cake upside down without affecting its shape. This prevents shrinking.

- Adding small amount of lemon juice or orange juice in the egg white batter adds flavours.

- It is easier when milk and eggs are at room temperature.

- Spray oil around chiffon mold so it does not stick too much

- Use plastic spoon/tool to remove chiffon from mold to not scratch the mold